$ ---- BCs ----
$ phi = 0 symmetry (XZ plane): nodes 1..5 ; Uy = Rx = Rz = 0
SPC1, 1, 246, 1, THRU, 5
$ phi = 90 symmetry (YZ plane): nodes 21..25 ; Ux = Ry = Rz = 0
SPC1, 1, 156, 21, THRU, 25
$ The two phi-symmetry SPCs leave Uz free (the loads are self-equilibrated
$ in X and Y, so Z is unconstrained). Anchor Uz at a single node at the
$ hole edge (node 1, theta=18, phi=0) to remove the Z rigid-body mode.
SPC1, 1, 3, 1
$ ---- loads ----
$ Outward load at the +X equator point (phi = 0, theta = 90), node 5:
$ half of P = 2.0 (cut by the phi=0 symmetry plane) -> 1.0 in +X.
FORCE, 1, 5, , 1.0, 1.0, 0.0, 0.0
$ Inward load at the +Y equator point (phi = 90, theta = 90), node 25:
$ half of P = 2.0 -> 1.0 in -Y.
FORCE, 1,25, , 1.0, 0.0,-1.0, 0.0
ENDDATA
